## Broken

| What | Effect | References |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **A card that is not valid UTF-8 stops the build.** The specification reports such a file as HMD019 and leaves it out; the loader decodes every card and fails on the first that will not decode | One stray file ends `build` with a decode error instead of an index without it [`vault.py`, `load`] | [[hmd-lang-spec#encoding]], [[hmd-0028#the-embedded-text]] |
| **A leading byte-order mark hides the frontmatter.** The specification ignores the mark; the loader needs the opening fence at byte 0, so a card saved with one loses its title and header | The card is indexed under the wrong text, and its content hash differs from the one `hmd` would agree with [`vault.py`, `split_header`] | [[hmd-lang-spec#encoding]], [[hmd-0028#the-embedded-text]] |
| **Names are not compared after NFC, lines split at more than the three CommonMark endings, and a shadowed card is indexed beside the card that shadows it.** `owl.hmd` and `owl.md` are both indexed as `owl`, where the specification binds the first and shadows the second | The index can hold two entries under one name, and a name written in another Unicode form is a different card [`vault.py`] | [[hmd-lang-spec#lexical-model]], [[hmd-lang-spec#resolving-a-reference-within-a-directory]] |

## Limitations (known gaps)

| Limitation | Why it stands | References |
| --- | --- | --- |
| The text contract is shared with HQL's loader, and a change to either must change both | The text this tool embeds and hashes has to be byte-identical to the text HQL hashes, so `vault.py` reimplements HQL's document loader and its frontmatter parser. Nothing in this repository runs HQL's loader, so a difference is caught only by HQL's own tests over its copy of the fixture vault | [[hmd-0028#the-embedded-text]] |
| The frontmatter parser is not a YAML parser | It is HQL's: block mappings, block and flow lists, and plain scalars. Frontmatter outside that subset is read as HQL reads it, which is the property that matters here | [[hmd-0028#the-embedded-text]] |
| An index answers only the queries it was built with | A reader has no model and cannot embed a question, so `build --query` embeds each one and a query the index does not hold is a failure at the reader | [[hmd-0028#schema-version-1]] |
| The committed fixture index names the tool's former name | It was built before the move and reads `hql-semantics 0.1.0`. Rebuilding needs the model, and no reader compares the string | [[hmd-0028#schema-version-1]] |
| The `local` provider is not exercised by a test | It needs `torch`, `transformers` and a checkpoint, which CI does not install. Its arithmetic is the pooling and normalising in `embed.py` | [[hmd-0028#the-embedder]] |
| `endpoint` and `api_key_env` are accepted and unused under `local` | The table is checked for what the chosen provider needs, and a key the provider does not use is left alone | [[hmd-0028#the-embedder]] |

## Done

- **`location_path` names the namespace root** — the builder reads the
  setting formerly called `wiki`, with the default `.`, the vault itself;
  released in 0.2.0.
- **Published to PyPI** — `release-semantics.yml` on a `semantics-vX.Y.Z` tag,
  trusted publishing, 0.1.0 [[hmd-0028#deployment--activation]].
- **The cards of the namespace root** — read from the directory `location_path` names,
  paths relative to it, `.md` and `.markdown` cards included and nested vaults left out, as HQL
  reads them [HMD-0029].

- **`build`** — every card of a vault and every `--query` embedded and written
  as schema version 1, with the build stamp pinnable so a rebuild of an
  unchanged vault is byte-identical [[hmd-0028#schema-version-1]].
- **`verify`** — stale cards, cards missing from either side, vectors of the
  wrong length, and vectors that are not unit length, with exit status 1.
- **`inspect`** — what an index says about itself.
- **`[semantics]` and `[semantics.embedder]`** — the index path held inside the
  vault, the `local` and `http` providers, flags over the table key by key, and
  the refusals: an unknown key, an unknown provider, a literal `api_key`, an
  `http` embedder without `endpoint`, `model` or `revision`
  [[hmd-0028#the-semantics-table]].
- **The package** — the distribution `hypermarkdown-semantics`, the command
  `hmd-semantics`, no dependency, and `torch` and `transformers` as the extra
  `local`.
- **A CI job** — the tests against the tool's committed lockfile, with no model
  framework installed.

## Gates

```bash
cd tools/hmd-semantics
uv sync --locked
uv run python -m pytest
```

## Open questions

None.

## Changelog

- 2026-11-24: a Done row for reading `location_path`, the `wiki` setting's new name.
- 2026-11-24: before the 0.1.0 release. Status names the released version and
  says how the tool stands to HyperMarkDown 0.1.0: it reads cards and does not
  implement the language. The Broken row about the cards location was fixed in
  0.1.0 and contradicted the Done row, so it is gone; in its place, three
  Broken rows for the 0.1 reading rules HQL's loader does not follow yet,
  found by running the loader on small trees. The question about publishing
  to PyPI is answered: 0.1.0 is there.

- 2026-11-15: reading cards from the vault itself moved from a limitation to
  broken: `wiki` is decided to stay as the cards location, so the walk is
  wrong where the two differ.
- 2026-11-15: created with the tool.
